\section{Status field gotcha}{

Record status is read from the plain-string \code{lifecycle} field (e.g.
\code{"done"}, \code{"in_progress"}). The handler deliberately does \strong{not} request
the \code{issueStatus} enum — it has a server-side serialization bug that returns
HTTP 500 for the whole query on some records.
}

\section{Geometry}{

\code{Issue.hasGeography} flags whether a record has a footprint;
\code{Issue.geographies} returns a GraphQL \code{FeatureCollection} whose per-feature
\code{geometry} arrives as a \strong{GeoJSON string} needing a second
\code{jsonlite::fromJSON} parse. Point / LineString / Polygon are all observed.
Coordinates are already geographic \strong{WGS84 (EPSG:4326 lon/lat)} — \emph{not} the
projected ISN93 grid — so no reprojection happens. When
\code{write_sidecar = TRUE}, the (re-parsed) geometry is saved next to the
sidecar as \verb{<document_id>.geometry.geojson} in the family FeatureCollection
layout (GeoJSON-2008 \code{crs} member naming \verb{urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::4326}); the
sidecar carries \code{geometry_path} and \code{geometry_crs} (\code{"EPSG:4326"}). Records
with \code{hasGeography = false} / an empty collection leave the geometry columns
\code{NA}.
}

\section{Attachments}{

Documents live under \verb{phases[].files[]}, each an \code{IssuePhaseFile} with a
semantic-role \code{type} and a nested \code{data} \verb{File \{ path, name, ... \}}. Only
files with \code{published == true} are emitted. They are grouped by their
\code{IssuePhaseFile.type} into lowercase slugs — \code{almennt} (general; incl. the
matsskýrsla / EIA report and matsáætlun), \code{vidbrogd} (developer responses),
and \code{afgreidsla} (the decision / álit) — one \verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} /
\verb{local_path_<slug>} list-column each, with the deduplicated union in
\code{attachment_urls} / \code{local_path} (required by the schema). The download URL
is \verb{https://www.skipulagsgatt.is/<File.path>} (path of the form
\verb{files/<uuid>}), anonymous. The top-level \code{Issue.files} collection is usually
empty and is ignored. PDFs are large (often 10-16 MB) — set
\code{max_file_size_mb} accordingly.
}

\section{Filter coverage (v0.1)}{

